---
import FutureTechMissionFrame from '../../../../components/FutureTechMissionFrame.astro';
---
<FutureTechMissionFrame
  missionNumber="2"
  title="Make It Think"
  tagline="Make your micro:bit remember, repeat, choose, and decide."
  question="How can code remember information, repeat actions, create unpredictable results, and make a decision?"
  success="I can use a variable, a simple loop, a random value, and one IF condition to control what happens."
>
  <section id="stage-1" class="stage"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">01</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">RECONNECT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Set Up</h2></div></div><p class="intro">Get your numbered kit and reopen your coding brain with a very quick Mission 1 reboot.</p><div class="check-list"><span>☐ Computer</span><span>☐ micro:bit</span><span>☐ USB data cable</span><span>☐ Mission page open</span></div><div class="step-card"><strong>Mission 1 Reboot</strong><p>Open your saved Mission 1 project <b>if it is easy to find</b>. Change what Button A displays, then test it in the simulator. If you cannot find it within 2 minutes, skip the reboot and continue.</p></div><p class="success"><b>Individual mission:</b> build, test, and explain your own code. Work with another student only for a brief troubleshooting check if TRY 4 sends you there.</p></section>
  <section id="stage-2" class="stage"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">02</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">REMEMBER</p><h2 class="stage-title">First Code — Variables</h2></div></div><p class="concept">A <b>variable</b> is information your program remembers. Think of it as a labelled memory box.</p><div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>1 — Open MakeCode</strong><p>Open <a class="external" href="https://makecode.microbit.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MakeCode for micro:bit ↗</a>. Choose <b>New Project</b>. Name it <code>FirstName_L1_M2</code>.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>2 — Create score</strong><p>Create a variable named <code>score</code>. In <code>on start</code>, use <code>set score to 0</code>.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>3 — Count up</strong><p>Button A: <code>change score by 1</code>, then <code>show number score</code>.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>4 — Count down</strong><p>Button B: <code>change score by -1</code>, then show the score.</p></article></div>
    <aside class="code-model" aria-label="Visual MakeCode model for score variable"><div class="code-model-head"><span>CODE MODEL</span><strong>Compare your score program to this</strong></div><div class="block-finder"><span><b>Variables</b> → Make a Variable</span><span><b>Variables</b> → set / change</span><span><b>Input</b> → on button pressed</span><span><b>Basic</b> → show number</span></div><div class="code-columns three"><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block event">on start</div><div class="mk-block variables indent">set <span class="value">score</span> to <span class="value">0</span></div></div><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block input">on button <span class="value">A</span> pressed</div><div class="mk-block variables indent">change <span class="value">score</span> by <span class="value">1</span></div><div class="mk-block basic indent">show number <span class="value">score</span></div></div><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block input">on button <span class="value">B</span> pressed</div><div class="mk-block variables indent">change <span class="value">score</span> by <span class="value">-1</span></div><div class="mk-block basic indent">show number <span class="value">score</span></div></div></div><p class="code-model-note">The key visual check: <b>SET</b> happens once at the start. Each button uses <b>CHANGE</b>, then displays the remembered score.</p></aside>
    <p class="success">✓ You should see: A makes the remembered score go up. B makes it go down.</p><p class="warning">Common bug: if the score always stays at 1, compare your blocks to the model and check whether you used <b>SET</b> instead of <b>CHANGE</b>.</p><div class="concept"><b>SET replaces. CHANGE adjusts.</b><br />If score = 4: SET score to 1 → 1. CHANGE score by 1 → 5.</div></section>
  <section id="stage-3" class="stage"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">03</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">REMEMBER → REPEAT → DECIDE → OUTPUT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Make It React</h2></div></div><div class="route"><span>INPUT: Shake</span><span>REMEMBER: Random number</span><span>REPEAT: Loop</span><span>DECIDE: IF question</span><span>OUTPUT: Result</span></div><div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>Challenge A — Random Choice</strong><p>Create a variable named <code>number</code>. On shake, set it to <code>pick random 1 to 6</code>, then show the number.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Challenge B — Decision: IF</strong><p>After showing the number, add <code>IF number = 6</code>. Inside the IF, add <code>repeat 3 times</code> and place a special icon or short flash inside the loop.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>What does RANDOM mean?</strong><p>Unpredictable does <b>not</b> mean always different. The same number can appear twice.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>What does a LOOP mean?</strong><p>A <b>loop</b> repeats instructions. <code>repeat 3 times</code> runs the blocks inside three times, then stops.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>What does IF mean?</strong><p>IF asks a yes/no question. <b>TRUE</b> → run the blocks inside. <b>FALSE</b> → skip them.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Read the order</strong><p>Choose the random number first → check the IF → if true, run the looped special response.</p></article></div>
    <aside class="code-model" aria-label="Visual MakeCode model for random number, IF condition, and repeat loop"><div class="code-model-head"><span>CODE MODEL</span><strong>Read this from top to bottom</strong></div><div class="block-finder"><span><b>Input</b> → on shake</span><span><b>Variables</b> → set</span><span><b>Math</b> → pick random</span><span><b>Basic</b> → show number / icon</span><span><b>Logic</b> → if / =</span><span><b>Loops</b> → repeat</span></div><div class="code-columns one"><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block input">on shake</div><div class="mk-block variables indent">set <span class="value">number</span> to <span class="inline-math">pick random 1 to 6</span></div><div class="mk-block basic indent">show number <span class="value">number</span></div><div class="mk-block logic indent">if <span class="value">number = 6</span> then</div><div class="mk-block loops indent2">repeat <span class="value">3</span> times</div><div class="mk-block basic indent3">show icon <span class="value">★</span></div></div></div><div class="logic-preview"><span><b>If number = 4</b> → show 4, skip the special loop.</span><span><b>If number = 6</b> → show 6, then repeat the special icon 3 times.</span></div><p class="code-model-note">The nesting matters: the <b>repeat</b> block sits inside the <b>IF</b>, and the special output sits inside the <b>repeat</b>.</p></aside>
    <p class="concept">Predict before testing: What happens if <code>number = 4</code>? What happens if <code>number = 6</code>?</p><p class="success">Shake several times. If 6 does not appear, explain when the repeated special response <i>would</i> happen and keep moving.</p><p class="warning">Order matters: choose the random number first, then check the IF condition. The repeat loop belongs inside the special response. If it does not work, use TRY 4 and compare the nesting to the model.</p></section>
  <section id="stage-4" class="stage"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">04</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">YOUR CREATION</p><h2 class="stage-title">Build It — Chance Machine</h2></div></div><p class="intro">Create a Chance Machine that chooses a random result, checks one condition, and repeats a special response when that condition is true.</p><div class="check-list"><span>☐ A named variable stores the random value</span><span>☐ The program uses an input event</span><span>☐ It has a visible output</span><span>☐ It uses one IF condition</span><span>☐ The special result uses one repeat loop</span><span>☐ The value is chosen before the condition is checked</span><span>☐ It runs on the real micro:bit</span><span>☐ You changed the range, repeated effect, result, icon, message, or theme</span></div><p class="mini-label">Choose a theme or invent your own</p><div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>Lucky Number</strong><p>Shake 1–6. One number triggers a repeated celebration.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Treasure Hunt</strong><p>Shake 1–5. One value discovers the treasure and flashes the result.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Critical Hit</strong><p>Shake 1–10. The highest value triggers a repeated special attack.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Mystery Machine</strong><p>Create a different random theme with one special repeated outcome.</p></article></div><div class="try4"><strong>STUCK? TRY 4</strong><p>1. CHECK — compare your blocks and nesting to the code model. 2. SIMULATE the newest code. 3. DOWNLOAD the newest version. 4. PARTNER — briefly explain expected vs actual to a nearby student. Still stuck? Ask for help and say what you already tried.</p></div></section>
  <section id="stage-5" class="stage"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">05</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">OPTIONAL CHALLENGE</p><h2 class="stage-title">Level It Up</h2></div></div><p class="intro">Only after the Chance Machine works. Choose one while you wait for your checkpoint.</p><div class="level-grid"><article class="level-card"><strong>Try Again</strong><p>Add ELSE so the program gives a different response when the IF is false.</p></article><article class="level-card"><strong>Change the Odds</strong><p>Change the random range. Decide whether the special result is more or less likely.</p></article><article class="level-card"><strong>Two Special Results</strong><p>Add another IF condition for a second special value.</p></article><article class="level-card"><strong>Keep Score</strong><p>Add a <code>wins</code> variable and increase it when the special result happens.</p></article></div><p class="success">When every Build It box is checked, add your name to the Ready-for-Check queue. Keep Leveling Up until you are called.</p></section>
  <section id="stage-6" class="stage checkpoint"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">06</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SHOW WHAT YOU KNOW</p><h2 class="stage-title">Checkpoint</h2></div></div><p class="intro">Bring your micro:bit and open your code when you are called. Each student completes the checkpoint individually.</p><div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>Check 1 — Remember It</strong><p>Point to one variable. Explain what information it remembers and give one value it could hold.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Check 2 — Explain the Decision + Loop</strong><p>Point to your IF condition and repeat loop. Explain when the IF is true and what the loop repeats.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Check 3 — Change It</strong><p>Change the winning value, repeat count, random range, or special output. Then test it.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>After Your Check</strong><p><b>MISSION COMPLETE</b> · <b>RETRY ONE SKILL</b> · <b>SUPPORT ROUTE</b></p></article></div></section>
  <section class="stage passport"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">✓</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SKILL PASSPORT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Mission 2 Skills</h2></div></div><div class="check-list"><span>☐ I can create and use a variable</span><span>☐ I can change a variable's value</span><span>☐ I can use a simple repeat loop</span><span>☐ I can generate a random value</span><span>☐ I can use one IF condition</span><span>☐ I can change, test, and explain my code</span></div></section>
  <section class="stage reset"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">↺</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">LEAVE IT READY</p><h2 class="stage-title">Reset</h2></div></div><div class="check-list"><span>☐ Project saved correctly</span><span>☐ micro:bit back in the numbered kit</span><span>☐ USB cable loosely coiled</span><span>☐ Kit complete and workspace clear</span><span>☐ Damage or missing equipment reported</span></div><p class="concept">Exit question: What is one thing your program remembered, repeated, or decided today?</p></section>
</FutureTechMissionFrame>
<style is:global>
.code-model{margin:.8rem 0;padding:.9rem;border:1px solid #c7d2fe;border-radius:15px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f8faff,#f5f3ff)}.code-model-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:.75rem;align-items:center;margin-bottom:.55rem}.code-model-head span{color:#6d28d9;font:900 .66rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.09em}.code-model-head strong{color:#26324a;font-size:.9rem}.block-finder{display:flex;gap:.4rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:.7rem}.block-finder span{padding:.34rem .5rem;border:1px solid #dbe3ef;border-radius:999px;background:#fff;color:#52617a;font-size:.72rem;font-weight:750}.block-finder b{color:#5b21b6}.code-columns{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.7rem;align-items:start}.code-columns.one{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,600px)}.code-columns.three{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr))}.code-stack{display:grid;gap:.28rem;padding:.65rem;border-radius:12px;background:#111827}.mk-block{width:max-content;max-width:100%;padding:.48rem .62rem;border-radius:7px;color:#fff;font:800 .76rem/1.25 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;box-shadow:inset 0 -2px rgba(0,0,0,.16)}.mk-block.event{background:#7c3aed}.mk-block.input{background:#c026d3}.mk-block.basic{background:#2563eb}.mk-block.variables{background:#dc2626}.mk-block.logic{background:#0f766e}.mk-block.loops{background:#15803d}.mk-block.indent{margin-left:1rem}.mk-block.indent2{margin-left:2rem}.mk-block.indent3{margin-left:3rem}.mk-block .value{display:inline-block;margin-left:.18rem;padding:.05rem .3rem;border-radius:4px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.2)}.mk-block .inline-math{display:inline-block;margin-left:.18rem;padding:.05rem .3rem;border-radius:4px;background:#6d28d9}.logic-preview{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:.45rem;margin-top:.6rem}.logic-preview span{padding:.55rem .65rem;border:1px solid #d9e3ef;border-radius:9px;background:#fff;color:#536177;font-size:.78rem;line-height:1.4}.logic-preview b{color:#26324a}.code-model-note{margin:.6rem 0 0;color:#59677c;font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.45}.code-model-note b{color:#37205f}@media(max-width:820px){.code-columns.three{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:680px){.code-model-head{display:grid}.code-columns,.code-columns.one,.code-columns.three,.logic-preview{grid-template-columns:1fr}.mk-block{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}.mk-block.indent{width:calc(100% - .55rem);margin-left:.55rem}.mk-block.indent2{width:calc(100% - 1.1rem);margin-left:1.1rem}.mk-block.indent3{width:calc(100% - 1.65rem);margin-left:1.65rem}}
</style>
